Q: jQuery Animate table &lt;td&gt; elements when changing colspan values for them A: <p>Make additional table columns. Include some of them in some <code>colspan</code>s and others in other <code>colspan</code>s (this might require for example replacing some implicit <code>colspan=&quot;1&quot;</code> by explicit <code>colspan=&quot;2&quot;</code>). Animate the increase of the <code>width</code> of some columns from <code>0</code> and the reduction of the <code>width</code> of other columns to <code>0</code>.</p>
<p>Here's a rough sketch:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.shrink { width: 200px; }
.grow { width: 0; }

body:has(#new:checked) .shrink { width: 0; }
body:has(#new:checked) .grow { width: 200px; }

td {
  transition: width linear 2s;
  border: 1px solid black;
  padding: 0;
}
table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;td colspan="2" style="background:#bb8"&gt;This cell will seem to change its colspan&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td class="shrink"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;Text&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td class="grow" colspan="2"&gt;Text&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;label&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="new" checked&gt;Click here to toggle apparent colspan&lt;/label&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<ul>
<li>To make the size changes uniform (without weird changes of speed), take <code>clientWidth</code> of the elements into account and construct <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/easing-function/linear" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>linear()</code></a> with several keypoints, I guess.
<ul>
<li>Making the transition nonlinear makes things more complicated:
<ul>
<li>Approximate a nonlinear transition with a piecewise linear one (<code>linear()</code> with many keypoints).</li>
<li>Or turn the transition into an animation and scrub through it with <code>requestAnimationFrame()</code>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
